   "subject": "Re: oSCR sex ratio??",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Rachel, <div><br></div><div>In oSCR, you will get an estimate of the probability that an individual selected at random is a male, *on the link scale*, so in effect is the proportion of the population that is male. The formula you cite is a standard one and will give you the sex ration, as long as you back-transform the estimate to the probability scale. </div><div><br></div><div>Hope that helps.</div><div><br></div><div>Chris <br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
